{
"_note": "Legal-form suffixes. 'pattern' is a regex matched at the end of a name (or anywhere when 'anywhere' is true); 'cs' = case-sensitive; 'in' refines the form by jurisdiction (e.g. 'Corporation' of a Japanese company is a kabushiki kaisha). The longest matching suffix wins.",
"forms": {
  "JP-KK": {"type": "Kabushiki kaisha (joint-stock company)", "countries": ["JP"]},
  "JP-GK": {"type": "Godo kaisha (limited liability company)", "countries": ["JP"]},
